WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.089
Choose the metrics that matter
This profile follows a synthetic refund assistant.

00:00:03.089 --> 00:00:10.880
Start with the profile configuration
We selected runs, steps, rule violations and failed refunds.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:18.943
Define what a metric measures
Failed refunds counts steps whose outcome is failed.

00:00:18.943 --> 00:00:27.711
See the configured metrics in action
The results come from the recorded workflow history.

00:00:27.711 --> 00:00:34.111
Delivery Health: 94 out of 100
All runs completed. Earlier failures still affect delivery health.

00:00:34.111 --> 00:00:40.680
Completion and rule compliance are separate
A completed run can still have recorded approval violations.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.304
Open the runs behind the numbers
Follow the profile history into an individual execution.

00:00:43.304 --> 00:00:54.030
Inspect a recovered run
This refund completed after a failed attempt and a fresh approval.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.575
Keep the earlier failure visible
Open the failed step to inspect its recorded details.

00:00:57.575 --> 00:01:04.265
Inspect the context behind an attempt
The amount, currency and payment reference stay attached to the step.

00:01:04.265 --> 00:01:10.699
Configured metrics. Connected evidence.
Choose what to measure, review health, then inspect the underlying runs.
